> 
> Unfortunately, I haven't found an altar yet. But I do have my pet dog
> from level 1 with me, whom I use to check for BUC status, the "moves
> only reluctantly" hint. I am not sure how reliable that method is but
> in my experience, it has served me very well and so far, without
> exception. I usually litter the items of potential interest around me,
> put my pet dog on a leash and wait several turns so that my dogs
> happily runs around me and I keep a eye on the "moves only
> reluctantly" messages. Is that a reasonable way to do it?

If the dogs steps on an item reluctantly it's cursed, if it steps on
any item without that message then it's either uncursed or blessed.
(Advanced information: a few items in Nethack auto-curse if picked up
or if worn; one sort of a helmet, a pointy cap, and one sort of grey
stone which you typically can find in the mines.)

> That brings out a question I had in mind, do cursed items *always*
> weld themselves to the wearer?

Weapons, armour, amulets, rings: yes. Cursed wands can explode, IIRC,
but it doesn't happen often. Don't read cursed books. Cursed food can
have bad effects when eaten, quaffed cursed potions and read cursed
scrolls not the expected effect, often worse. (Advanced information:
depending on whether you are confused or not the effects may change,
even to something advantageous.)

> If yes, then all the armor I have is
